{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/qgwli5","slide":1,"text":"This slide explains why the design is intentionally minimal. The experiment is not trying to vary the game, the payoff structure, or the quality of the AI analysis at the same time. Those are held constant. What changes is the responsibility architecture around the same decision. That is why the comparison is cleaner: if outcomes differ across conditions, the interpretation is not that one AI answer was better than another. It is that different accountability interventions changed how participants understood ownership, visibility, and responsibility."}
