{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/iub8n9","slide":2,"text":"This is the mechanism slide. The paper is not saying that AI directly makes people escalate. The proposed chain is more specific. First, the system intervention changes the accountability environment. For example, disclosure changes visibility and traceability, while confirmation changes whether the human actively passes through the AI stage. Second, these structural changes may change subjective responsibility, such as felt accountability, decisional ownership, and responsibility sharing. Third, if those responsibility perceptions change, they may affect whether participants choose escalation or restraint."}
